&lt;li&gt;Contribute C++ code when required for low-level testing, tooling, or integration support&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Analyze robot behavior and system performance, identifying root causes for issues related to kinematics, motion planning, control, perception, or hardware interaction&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Evaluate and debug complex robotic behaviors such as singularities, joint limit violations, trajectory instabilities, and configuration inconsistencies&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Work with URDF models, coordinate transformations, and robot descriptions to validate system correctness&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Support development and refinement of application demos, internal showcases, and customer-facing use cases• Collaborate closely with software, electronics, controls, and mechanical teams to reproduce issues and validate fixes&lt;/li&gt;
